  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is the smallest equivalence relation on the set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>}</mo></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>{</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>}</mo><mo>⊂</mo><mi>R</mi></math>, then the number of elements in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> is ______.",
    "image": null
  },
